failure_location.quote:
or the regularized approximant \eqref{eq:regularized_mcemdmd}, i.e.,
\begin{align*}
    \widehat \calK^{\mathrm{MC}}f = f_\calX^\top (\mathbf{K}_{\calX}^{-1} + \lambda I)^{-1}\bbK_{\calX, \calY}^{\mathrm{MC}} (\mathbf{K}_{\calX} + \lambda I)^{-1}\bbk_\calX.
\end{align*}

For the unregularized inverse, the bound
\(
    \max_{v\in\one} v^\top \mathbf K_{\mathcal X}^{-1} v \leq \frac{d}{\lambda_\mathrm{min}(\mathbf{K}_\calX)}
\)
 and $\lambda_\mathrm{min}(\mathbf{K}_\calX) = O(h_\calX^{3})  = O(d^{-3})$ give
\begin{align*}
    \left(
      \max_{v\in\one} v^\top \mathbf K_{\mathcal X,\lambda}^{-1} v
    \right)^{1/2} = O\left( \sqrt{\frac{d}{d^{-3}}}\right) = O(d^2) = O(h_\calX^{-2}).
\end{align*}
